# Line-ending policy for this repo.
#
# Everything is stored as LF and checked out as LF, regardless of the committing
# client's OS or its `core.autocrlf` setting. This repo builds and runs on Linux
# (CI) as well as Windows, and some artifacts are byte-compared across platforms
# — the `.phys` conformance corpus and cross-language determinism fixtures. A
# CRLF working copy on one machine and LF on another turns those into spurious
# diffs.
#
# The index here already contains zero CRLF files, so this is a no-op for existing
# content; it just makes the guarantee explicit and silences the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are parsed by cmd.exe, which is genuinely CRLF-sensitive
# (labels and `goto` can misbehave with LF).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary — never diffed, never normalized.
*.glb     binary
*.phys    binary
*.npz     binary
*.parquet binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.ico     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.pdf     binary
*.mp4     binary
*.tar.gz  binary
*.zip     binary
